## Real Root Cause

In [output.py](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/rw5_sqlparse/sqlparse/filters/output.py#L80-L127), `OutputPHPFilter._process` serializes SQL tokens inside PHP **double-quoted** string literals (`"..."` at lines 93, 100, 108, 126), while line 120 escapes only `\` and `"`. PHP evaluates variable and complex-expression interpolation (`$name`, `${expr}`, `{$obj->prop}`, `{${...}}`) inside double-quoted strings whenever an unescaped `$` appears.

Observed output from `sqlparse.format(sql, output_format='php')` (verified on `sqlparse` `0.6.1.dev0`, [__init__.py](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/rw5_sqlparse/sqlparse/__init__.py#L16)):

| SQL Input | Current PHP Output | Risk in PHP |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `SELECT '$name'` | `$sql = "SELECT '$name'";` | Variable interpolation (`$name`) |
| `SELECT '${expr}'` | `$sql = "SELECT '${expr}'";` | Complex expression interpolation (`${expr}`) |
| `SELECT '{$obj->prop}'` | `$sql = "SELECT '{$obj->prop}'";` | Curly expression interpolation (`{$obj->prop}`) |
| `SELECT $body$text$body$` | `$sql = "SELECT $body$text$body$";` | Variable interpolation (`$body`, `$body`) |
| `SELECT '\$name'` | `$sql = "SELECT '\\$name'";` | Escaped `\` + active interpolation (`$name`) |

---

## Minimal Recommended Fix

Escape `$` as `\$` **after** escaping `\` as `\\` in `OutputPHPFilter._process` ([output.py](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/rw5_sqlparse/sqlparse/filters/output.py#L116-L120)). Do not touch `OutputPythonFilter` or `lexer.py`.

```diff
--- a/sqlparse/filters/output.py
+++ b/sqlparse/filters/output.py
@@ -113,11 +113,15 @@ class OutputPHPFilter(OutputFilter):
                     yield sql.Token(T.Whitespace, after_lb)
                 continue
 
-            # Escape backslashes before quotes so a backslash preceding a
-            # quote cannot break out of the generated string literal
-            # (GHSA-3496-9g83-7v6x).
+            # Escape backslashes before quotes and dollar signs so a backslash
+            # cannot break out of the generated double-quoted string literal
+            # (GHSA-3496-9g83-7v6x) or leave a `$` unescaped for PHP
+            # variable/expression interpolation.
             else:
-                token.value = token.value.replace('\\', '\\\\').replace('"', '\\"')
+                token.value = (
+                    token.value.replace('\\', '\\\\')
+                    .replace('"', '\\"')
+                    .replace('$', '\\$')
+                )
 
             # Put the token
             yield sql.Token(T.Text, token.value)
```

### Why Escape Order Matters
- **`\` must be escaped first.** Escaping `$` before `\` turns `$name` into `\$name` and then `\\$name`, which in PHP evaluates to a literal backslash followed by an interpolated `$name` variable—completely defeating the fix.
- With `\` escaped first, then `"` and `$`:
  - `'$name'` → `'\$name'`
  - `'${expr}'` → `'\${expr}'`
  - `'{$obj->prop}'` → `'{\$obj->prop}'` (`{` only starts complex interpolation when immediately followed by an unescaped `$`)
  - `$body$text$body$` → `\$body\$text\$body\$`
  - `'\$name'` → `'\\\$name'`
  - `'\\$name'` → `'\\\\\$name'`
- `varname` (`$sql`) is emitted outside the string literal at [output.py](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/rw5_sqlparse/sqlparse/filters/output.py#L81), [output.py](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/rw5_sqlparse/sqlparse/filters/output.py#L87), and [output.py](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/rw5_sqlparse/sqlparse/filters/output.py#L104), so it remains intact.

### Verification Status
- **Verified:** Tokenization (`sqlparse.lexer.tokenize`), formatted output (`sqlparse.format(..., output_format='php'|'python')`, with and without `reindent=True`), and the proposed `replace` chain were executed in `python3`.
- **Not run:** End-to-end execution under a `php` runtime (`php` binary is not installed in this environment); PHP double-quoted string semantics were verified by specification and should be confirmed in CI/tests alongside unit tests for all five reporter payloads plus `'\\$name'`.

